caption: Psychic Patterns
tradition-component: psychic-patterns

A Psychic Pattern is a recorded supernatural profile that defines a legal prey category. A Dreadhound may create a Pattern after one or more of the following:

Successfully affecting the subject with an information-gathering psionic ability.

Successfully resisting one of the subject's supernatural abilities.

Examining a meaningful direct connection to the subject, including psychic residue or a physical specimen.

Completing a successful investigation that identifies the subject's supernatural Species, template, lineage, or Origin.

Each Pattern must identify one objective prey category: one individual; one supernatural Species or template; one specific supernatural lineage; or, after Mastery, one entire structural Origin. Political affiliation, nationality, ethnicity, personal dislike, and other voluntary social categories are never valid Patterns.

Creating a Pattern normally requires one hour of analysis and a successful roll against the best applicable Hidden Lore, Psychology, Physiology, Thaumatology, or Expert Skill, modified by the quality of the evidence. A direct supernatural encounter or complete specimen gives no penalty. Partial residue or secondhand records may impose ordinary task penalties. Failure wastes the analysis time but does not consume the evidence.
